From: =?UTF-8?q?Michel=20D=C3=A4nzer?= <mdaenzer@redhat.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 15:48:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] kms/crtc: Clamp max dispatch duration minus
 DEADLINE_EVASION_CONSTANT_US

Otherwise the largest clamped value results in
meta_kms_crtc_determine_deadline always considering the deadline missed
and skipping one refresh cycle.

Part-of: <https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/merge_requests/5116>
---
 src/backends/native/meta-kms-crtc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/native/meta-kms-crtc.c b/src/backends/native/meta-kms-crtc.c
index 8d9692ce4e9..70cefbed6a6 100644
--- a/src/backends/native/meta-kms-crtc.c
+++ b/src/backends/native/meta-kms-crtc.c
@@ -1073,7 +1073,8 @@ meta_kms_crtc_update_shortterm_max_dispatch_duration (MetaKmsCrtc *crtc,
     (int64_t) (0.5 + G_USEC_PER_SEC /
                meta_calculate_drm_mode_refresh_rate (&crtc->current_state.drm_mode));
 
-  crtc->shortterm_max_dispatch_duration_us = MIN (duration_us, refresh_interval_us);
+  crtc->shortterm_max_dispatch_duration_us =
+    MIN (duration_us, refresh_interval_us - DEADLINE_EVASION_CONSTANT_US);
 }
 
 int64_t
